DLP Lab: administrator-managed endpoint agent
=============================================

Install the native Debian 12 or 13 package with apt, then run:
  sudo dlp-setup connection.json

The private per-device profile contains its HTTPS registration and public CA.
It is prepared by the administrator, never contains the server admin token,
and must have mode0600. Desktop user and standard Telegram/Signal paths are
detected; --user and --telegram allow explicit selection when needed.

Setup preserves existing configuration, starts files/session/forwarder services,
and checks their status plus the fixed restart broker. No nested apt is invoked.
For an already configured endpoint: sudo dlp-setup (no profile required).
If /etc/dlp-lab/connection.json is provisioned before installation, postinst
runs setup automatically. Failure leaves the package installed and prints the
retry command; it does not claim protection is ready.

Debian12 requires SQLCipher4 from the project dependency package or a trusted
repository providing it; stock SQLCipher3 cannot read the supported Signal DB.

Service running does not prove field access or event delivery. Check the device
in the central panel and perform a synthetic file test. Session status may be
waiting_field until a supported focused text field is available.

Configuration and CLI are administrator-owned. The desktop user only receives
notifications. CLI manual administration uses sudo; no local control panel.
Source and current operations guide: https://github.com/Daret228/dlp-lab
